/-!
# Source-generated contribution-capacity settlement compiler

Settlement uses the existing reopening world.  Its initial target support is
the live three-row coface support.  The first compiler step is a complete
identity write on that ledger; the second is a faithful terminal generated by
three exact incidence events.  A later terminal handoff may use the old coface
face, whose complete ledger contains exactly the two inherited rows.

The ambient support-settlement receipt erases to the pre-existing disposition
type.  Authority remains in the private, source-event-indexed terminal
incidence event compiled by `LedgerTerminalRowSourceAt`; no receipt registry or
parallel lifecycle state is introduced here.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace ProcessGame
namespace Society
namespace M14SourceGeneratedContributionCapacitySettlementCompiler

noncomputable section

open ResponsibilityLifecycle LivingLawEvolution ConstructiveRoot
open ObstructionGeneratedMinimalCoface
